1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:06,084
EY Internal Audit Follow-Up is your governed workspace for tracking findings through to closure.

2
00:00:06,114 --> 00:00:12,726
Monitoring every commitment, testing whether the control now operates, and answering questions across the tested population.

3
00:00:12,756 --> 00:00:16,716
Two modes, one foundation. Here they are - on a single finding.

4
00:00:16,746 --> 00:00:18,622
Start with the work that repeats.

5
00:00:18,652 --> 00:00:23,392
The agent runs on a schedule internal audit sets, under rules internal audit approves.

6
00:00:23,422 --> 00:00:28,918
It ran at 03:14 this morning and built the register - 148 open commitments.

7
00:00:29,138 --> 00:00:30,582
23 overdue.

8
00:00:30,612 --> 00:00:34,584
14 where closure was withheld, because the evidence didn't support it.

9
00:00:34,614 --> 00:00:36,682
Those 37 go to a human.

10
00:00:36,712 --> 00:00:39,324
The other 111 closed on their own.

11
00:00:39,354 --> 00:00:41,406
The agent isn't replacing judgement.

12
00:00:41,436 --> 00:00:43,168
It's deciding what deserves it.

13
00:00:43,338 --> 00:00:46,754
Take the top one. RM-0412.

14
00:00:46,784 --> 00:00:50,036
Approval before works commence on all variations.

15
00:00:50,066 --> 00:00:53,334
Management says it's implemented, and wants it closed.

16
00:00:53,554 --> 00:00:55,670
Here's what management submitted.

17
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:58,408
A revised approval policy issued in June.

18
00:00:58,438 --> 00:01:02,110
A governance briefing, 31 attendees. Both real.

19
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:05,760
In most processes, this is where somebody ticks the box.

20
00:01:05,980 --> 00:01:07,808
The agent withheld closure.

21
00:01:08,578 --> 00:01:11,718
Its instruction was not to confirm that action was taken.

22
00:01:11,748 --> 00:01:14,088
It was to confirm that the control operates.

23
00:01:14,118 --> 00:01:16,474
The documents prove a policy exists.

24
00:01:16,504 --> 00:01:18,892
So the agent re-ran the original test.

25
00:01:18,922 --> 00:01:21,550
9 variations since 30 June.

26
00:01:21,580 --> 00:01:24,192
4 still approved after works had commenced.

27
00:01:24,712 --> 00:01:27,680
The policy exists. The control does not.

28
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:30,248
That's the work that repeats.

29
00:01:30,278 --> 00:01:36,622
Now the work nobody scheduled - the auditor, mid-fieldwork, asking something this agent was never built to answer.

30
00:01:36,742 --> 00:01:38,810
5 comparable contracts.

31
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:40,700
61 new exceptions.

32
00:01:40,730 --> 00:01:43,358
$940,000 at risk.

33
00:01:43,388 --> 00:01:45,984
None of which anyone had gone looking for.

34
00:01:46,204 --> 00:01:47,856
That took eight seconds.

35
00:01:47,886 --> 00:01:51,954
In most organisations it takes three weeks - because it isn't a question.

36
00:01:51,984 --> 00:01:55,508
It's a data request, queued behind somebody else's.

37
00:01:55,728 --> 00:01:57,540
The evidence assembles itself.

38
00:01:57,570 --> 00:02:03,926
Variation orders, approval minutes, commencement records, the delegation matrix in force on each date.

39
00:02:03,956 --> 00:02:05,784
47 source documents.

40
00:02:06,104 --> 00:02:07,692
Read the line underneath.

41
00:02:07,722 --> 00:02:10,242
Population tested. Rule applied.

42
00:02:10,272 --> 00:02:15,048
Read-only, zero records modified. The one foundation - both modes.

43
00:02:15,078 --> 00:02:18,378
Without provenance, none of this is audit evidence.

44
00:02:18,648 --> 00:02:22,188
Then the auditor acts, from inside the same conversation.

45
00:02:22,218 --> 00:02:24,526
No second system, no re-keying.

46
00:02:24,746 --> 00:02:27,118
Scope extended across five contracts.

47
00:02:27,148 --> 00:02:29,840
Management notified, evidence attached.

48
00:02:29,870 --> 00:02:32,242
61 exceptions into the audit plan.

49
00:02:32,272 --> 00:02:33,508
And the fourth one -

50
00:02:33,628 --> 00:02:35,024
The rule is updated.

51
00:02:35,054 --> 00:02:38,914
Monthly now, across all 312 contracts.

52
00:02:38,944 --> 00:02:42,180
Breaches surface before certification, not at audit.

53
00:02:42,210 --> 00:02:46,134
The register moves from 148 to 209.

54
00:02:46,554 --> 00:02:48,898
Two modes - but not two silos.

55
00:02:48,928 --> 00:02:50,884
The agent handles what repeats.

56
00:02:50,914 --> 00:02:53,062
The conversation handles what's new.

57
00:02:53,092 --> 00:02:58,088
And what the auditor finds in conversation becomes what the agent watches from then on.

